(3. RETRIEVAL PROTOCOL) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Retrieval must be scoped, decomposed and evaluated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SOP-3.1  Query construction) Tj
T*
(   Construct queries from verified facts, not unsupported model output. Include treatment) Tj
T*
(   concept, diagnosis status, policy product, service date and decision question.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SOP-3.2  Mandatory subqueries) Tj
T*
(   Retrieve coverage grant, applicable exclusions, exceptions, waiting periods, document) Tj
T*
(   requirements and monetary limits separately.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SOP-3.3  Metadata filters) Tj
T*
(   Filter policy ID, plan, effective date, jurisdiction, member category and document status) Tj
T*
(   before semantic ranking.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SOP-3.4  Complete-section retrieval) Tj
T*
(   For lists, definitions and schedules, retrieve the full authoritative section or) Tj
T*
(   structured records rather than relying on top-k fragments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SOP-3.5  No-answer gate) Tj
T*
(   If no sufficiently relevant authoritative clause is found, return NOT_FOUND and route to) Tj
T*
(   manual policy review.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SOP-3.6  Conflicting evidence) Tj
T*
(   Return CONFLICTING_POLICY_EVIDENCE when clauses disagree or precedence cannot be) Tj
T*
(   resolved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
